  "rally_astroturfed_by_one_operator": "REJECTED: 232 distinct first funders/410 (c7) and 200/357 (late), exchange-dominated; nonce>=20 for 58%; ENS rate = population; sampled aged wallets have hundreds of heterogeneous txs; nonce-0 share in peak bins 205-211 is 12-28% and never dominates; known farms in this game show nonce0 94-100% and peel-funded 99%.",
  "exchange_funded_set_is_one_operator": "NOT SUPPORTED: exchange funding is neutral; the aged-wallet histories and 8% ENS rate make a bought-wallet farm of 400+ implausible; but ~17% of released ARE fresh recycling-chain wallets (see residual class).",
  "null_model_conditions_on_the_rally": "TRUE but does not rescue the rule: under any ordering of the observed amounts the rule flags the same number of wallets, so it has neither precision nor recall in that regime; farms inside the rally (0x3230466e x25, 0x2e0db3f8 x10, 0x2cff890f x7, 0xafef9294 chain) are caught only by accident and equally-shaped unflagged fresh wallets exist (1/4 controls farm-like).",
  "burst_carries_signal": "WEAK: burst z=3.75 under hour shuffle falls to z=1.33 under 10-min-bin shuffle (share and density co-peak); drip is BELOW null (z=-2.3..-2.5).",
  "density_not_hour_is_the_driver": "h39-40 have 0.05 share 71-81% but 0.28 joins/calendar-block -> 0 flagged; h34-35 share 69-89% at 1.84-2.34 joins/block -> 709 flagged; h36 share 42% at 1.16 -> 0. The saturation condition is min-amount share x joins/block, not hour>=24."
